config SPI_TELINK_B87
	bool "Telink TLSR8278 SPI master driver"
	default y
	depends on DT_HAS_TELINK_B87_SPI_ENABLED
	depends on CLOCK_CONTROL
	select PINCTRL
	help
	  The SPI master (DS-TLSR8278 7.4): modes 0-3, 8-bit frames, MSB
	  first, a clock of the system clock / ((divider + 1) * 2). The
	  master sends or receives an octet, not both: a transfer sends its
	  TX frames, then receives the RX frames that come after them; one
	  that would keep what comes in while it sends is refused. The chip
	  select is a GPIO or the master's own (active low). Its module clock
	  comes from the clock control driver (CLOCK_CONTROL, the clk node).
